Explanation of Vote at the Adoption of the Scope, Modalities, Format and Organization of the High-Level Conference on Rohingya Muslims and Other Minorities in Myanmar Resolution
Edward Heartney
Minister Counselor to ECOSOC
New York, New York
March 25, 2025
The United States welcomes the adoption of this resolution. We commend the leadership of Finland and Malaysia in facilitating the text.
Four years after the coup, Myanmar faces a dire humanitarian and human rights crisis that has brought untold suffering to its people. This conference offers an opportunity to strengthen international support for all ethnic minorities, including the Rohingya and members of other minority groups, as well as to chart a path forward for meeting those groups’ needs. This includes enhancing efforts to create a conducive environment for the return of refugees who have had to flee Myanmar, while addressing the root causes of the crisis. The United States strongly supports these efforts. At the same time, we underscore that nowhere in Myanmar is safe for returns as long as the military continues its widespread violence against the people of Myanmar, and we categorically reject any attempts to force refugees back to Myanmar until conditions for returns are met.
With respect to OP4, the United States endorses the call for various stakeholders to undertake initiatives prior to the conference in order to make a meaningful contribution to its outcome. The United States urges all those who will lead such initiatives to communicate their activities openly and transparently to ensure coordination and avoid duplication of efforts.
Lastly, the United States disassociates from OP9 of the text due to the language on gender parity. The United States strongly supports the protection of women and girls, the defense of their rights, and their empowerment. However, the United States opposes the use of quotas to achieve parity for women and girls. We regret that language on women’s and youth’s meaningful participation in the high-level conference was not incorporated into the text.
Thank you.
