AS DELIVERED
The United States thanks the members of the General Assembly for their engagement on the resolution and thanks in particular to the UAE for its facilitation.
We urge Kimberley Process participants to work towards reform of the Kimberley Process in order to ensure it remains relevant as the diamond supply chain continues to evolve, including through an expanded definition of conflict diamonds.
The United States believes that the focus of the current definition on “rebel groups,” is far too narrow and does not account for the wide range of actors misusing diamonds to advance conflict.
The 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the Sustainable Development Goals advance a program of soft global governance that is inconsistent with U.S. sovereignty and adverse to the rights and interests of Americans. The United States will no longer reaffirm them.
The United States opposes the SDGs, and therefore we dissociate from the four paragraphs, PP5, PP12, OP10, and OP16 that refer to the SDGs or the Agenda 2030.
