Jonathan Shrier
Acting Representative to the UN Economic and Social Council
New York, New York
March 12, 2025
AS DELIVERED
Thank you Ambassador Leendertse for convening today’s meeting, and thank you to the presenters especially the Ambassadors of Mali and Haiti, as well as the indefatigable Assistant Secretary-General for Peacebuilding Support.
We want the Peacebuilding Fund to move at the speed of relevance to steer outcomes toward meaningful and material conflict prevention and lasting peace.
The United States is currently conducting a review of our support to the United Nations. The review’s outcome will determine whether the actions of the Organization are serving American interests.
Madam Chair, assessed funding for the Peacebuilding Fund as part of the 2025 UN Regular Budget has recently provided a predictable baseline of support; however, approval of this funding in future annual budgets should not be considered a foregone conclusion.
We must see the concrete and high impact results achieved in expending these resources, taking into account their cost effectiveness.
At the same time, voluntary contributions should remain the primary source of PBF funding.
Finally, on this year’s Peacebuilding Architecture Review, we must collectively work towards strengthening the Commission and sharpening an integrated, strategic, and coherent approach to prevention and peacebuilding that will maximize efficiencies.
The efforts must remain grounded in supporting national strategies and efforts aimed at preventing the outbreak, escalation, and recurrence of conflict. Thank you.
